summary: ndc_t needs read access to sysctl_net_t paths under /proc/sys/net
description: |+
    SELinux policy is missing rules allowing ndc_t (entered via ndc_exec_t-labeled
    binaries such as bind's rndc) to access sysctl_net_t-labeled paths under
    /proc/sys/net. Without the fix, rndc triggers AVC denials when it reads
    /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_local_port_range (and opendir /proc/sys/net). The fix
    is tracked in SELINUX-7500 (commit c0361cb61).

contact: SELinux reproducer agent using Claude
component:
  - selinux-policy
test: ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - type: library
    name: /selinux-policy/Library/common
    nick: selinux-policy
  - gcc
  - policycoreutils
  - selinux-policy
  - selinux-policy-targeted
  - setools-console
  - util-linux
recommend:
  - audit
  - libselinux
  - libselinux-utils
environment:
    AVC_ERROR: +no_avc_check
duration: 10m
enabled: true
tag:
  - NoRHEL4
  - NoRHEL5
  - NoRHEL6
  - NoRHEL7
  - NoRHEL8
  - targeted
link:
  - verifies: https://issues.redhat.com/browse/RHEL-311393
  - relates: https://issues.redhat.com/browse/SELINUX-7500
adjust+:
  - enabled: false
    when: distro == rhel-4, rhel-5, rhel-6, rhel-7, rhel-8
    because: ndc_t sysctl_net_t gap first confirmed on RHEL 9 and RHEL 10; ndc_exec_t type absent on older releases
extra-summary: /CoreOS/selinux-policy/Regression/ndc-sysctl-net-and-similar
extra-task: /CoreOS/selinux-policy/Regression/ndc-sysctl-net-and-similar
